+## 8. Integration front: paused (measured state)
+
+The branch-only integration agent `c78f32d87043` resolved 22 of 35 conflicts across
+several runs, but the pinned-model endpoint (`opencode-go/longcat-2.5-preview-free`)
+repeatedly returned `upstream_endpoint_unavailable` after ~10 minutes of work each
+run. Per Constitution X the work paused visibly; no fallback model was used.
+
+Paused state (clone `/workspace/agent-195-integration/repo`, local only, nothing
+pushed): branch `integration/195-release-onto-main`, mid-merge against
+`a14856a3`, **13 conflicts unresolved**.
+
+Root difficulty (measured, not guessed): main and the release line independently
+**refactored the same test infrastructure in opposite directions**, so a faithful
+merge must reconcile two structures, e.g.:
+
+- `tests/capstore/harness/treeFixture.ts` (main) vs `tests/capstore/treeFixture.ts`
+  (release) — release flattened the `harness/` directory.
+- `tests/secret-url/outgoing/fixtures/index.ts` (main) vs `.../backend.ts`,
+  `.../harness.ts`, `.../queue.ts`, `.../contention-fixture.ts` (release) — release
+  split the barrel into files.
+- `src/backend/features/islands/tests/append/append.test.ts`: `../../index.ts` +
+  `../index.ts` (main) vs `../index.ts` + `./harness.ts` + `./raw.ts` (release).
+
+A naive union leaves duplicate fixtures and can breach the ten-entry-per-directory
+ceiling; a correct result requires choosing one structure and rewriting imports
+tree-wide, then a green full gate.
+
+Recommendation (strengthened): the wholesale release→main merge is **not** the
+right primary path. Prefer a **targeted landing of the in-scope Kawun board-13
+capability/policy work** (`src/grants/policy/*` and its tests) onto main via a
+focused front, leaving the divergent test-infra refactors out; or a decision that
+main has superseded the release line. Either is cheaper and safer than reconciling
+two opposite refactors against the production deploy branch.
+
+Next action: keep #195 open; revisit with a dedicated front when the pinned-model
+endpoint is stable, or on the Founder's decision.
